{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 15, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III was born in 1140 and succeeded his father as count at the age of 12 after his father's assassination in 1152.\n\n*Early Life and Reign*\nRaymond III was still a minor when he became count and the regency was held by his mother Hodierna. During this time the county of Tripoli was threatened by the expanding power of Nur ad-Din the atabeg of Aleppo. In 1153 Raymond III was knighted by Baldwin III of Jerusalem and became a vassal of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He also married Eschiva of Bures the widow of Walter of Saint-Omer.\n\n*Capture and Imprisonment*\nIn 1164 Raymond III was captured by the forces of Nur ad-Din during the Battle of Harim. He was held captive for ten years and was released in 1174 after the death of Nur ad-Din. During his captivity the county of Tripoli was governed by his mother Hodierna.\n\n*Later Life and Reign*\nAfter his release from captivity Raymond III returned to Tripoli and resumed his rule. He played an important role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and was a key advisor to King Baldwin IV. In 1180 he was appointed as the regent of the kingdom and played a crucial role in the Battle of Belvoir in 1182. Raymond III died in 1187 without any heirs and the county of Tripoli passed to his nephew Bohemond IV of Antioch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004263356793671846}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.2455112934112549}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.07054182887077332}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0162071343511343}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.576279254957626e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.000